---
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';
import NetLab from '../components/NetLab.astro';
import {faqs} from '../lib/faqs.mjs';
import {NETS,netCounts} from '../lib/nets.mjs';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Printable Nets of 3D Shapes: Cube, Prism & Pyramid (Free)" headline="Printable nets of 3D shapes" section="Printables" description="Free printable nets of 3D shapes: cube, rectangular and triangular prism, pyramid, cylinder, cone and more. Set the size and glue tabs, then print at 100%."><Breadcrumbs items={[['Printables','/printable-nets/']]}/><div class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">A hands-on kind of geometry · from a flat page to a solid idea</div><h1>Printable nets of 3D shapes: cube, rectangular prism &amp; square pyramid</h1><p>Free to print for class or home, with no account needed. Choose a cube, rectangular prism, triangular or hexagonal prism, square pyramid, tetrahedron, octahedron, cylinder, or cone net, set its size in millimeters, then print, cut, and fold. Every net has dashed fold lines, labeled faces, and optional glue tabs.</p></div></div><section class="no-print" aria-labelledby="net-gallery-heading"><h2 id="net-gallery-heading">Choose a 3D shape net to print</h2><div class="net-gallery">{Object.entries(NETS).map(([shape,net])=><article class="net-card"><a href={`/printable-nets/${net.slug}/`}><img src={`/nets/${net.file}.svg`} width="190" height="250" loading="lazy" alt={`Printable ${net.title.toLowerCase()} net with labeled faces, dashed fold lines, and glue tabs`}/></a><h3><a href={`/printable-nets/${net.slug}/`}>{net.title} net</a></h3><p><strong>{netCounts(shape)}.</strong> {net.text}</p><div class="net-actions"><a href={`/printable-nets/${net.slug}/`}>Folding steps &amp; surface area</a><a href="#net-lab" data-pick={shape}>Customize the size</a><a href={`/nets/${net.file}.svg`} download={`geometry-lab-${net.file}.svg`}>Download SVG</a></div></article>)}</div></section><AdSlot type="rectangle"/><NetLab/><div class="explanation"><h2>Cut, fold, connect.</h2><ol><li>Cut along the solid outline, including any glue tabs.</li><li>Fold inward along each dashed line.</li><li>Apply glue to the tabs and bring neighboring faces together.</li></ol><p>For the pyramid, “slant height” is the altitude of a triangular face. It must be greater than half the base width to create a non-flat pyramid. For the cone, slant height is measured along the side and must be greater than the radius. Each net’s own page lists its pieces, folding steps, and the surface area worked out from the net.</p></div><noscript>Enable JavaScript to change the size or tabs. The cube net above prints at 30 mm, and each net in the gallery can be downloaded as an SVG.</noscript><div class="no-print"><div class="related"><a href="/shapes/cuboid/">Rectangular prism formulas ↗</a><a href="/learn/volume-and-surface-area/">Volume & surface area ↗</a><a href="/volume-calculator/">Volume calculator ↗</a></div><Faq items={faqs['printable-nets']} title="Printable nets: common questions"/></div></Layout>
